      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceutils_1a3b7ce3bb0f4ad8c679ddbf31a568823f" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::string</type>
        <definition>std::string utils::generate_uuid_v7</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>generate_uuid_v7</name>
        <qualifiedname>utils::generate_uuid_v7</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Generate a time-ordered UUID v7 string (RFC 9562). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The UUID encodes the current Unix timestamp in milliseconds in the most-significant 48 bits, followed by the version nibble (7), 12 random bits, the 2-bit variant (0b10), and 62 random bits.</para>
<para>UUID v7 values generated within the same process are monotonically increasing: two calls within the same millisecond yield the same timestamp portion, with the random suffix providing uniqueness.</para>
<para>Format: &quot;xxxxxxxx-xxxx-7xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx&quot; where the first 48 bits encode unix_ts_ms and y ∈ {8,9,a,b}.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Lowercase UUID v7 string. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
